{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794510935,"nonce":"AexJV9dtZIBfHCUi7xPm1brkyiM=","title":"Reported 2026-11-12 from a Scarab 0.4.0 install on EKS 1.35 with Karpenter v1 (scarab-server 0.4.0@sha256:004b3c9b…).","message":"A step Pod that needs a new node is failed as Unschedulable within about a second. On a cluster whose CI node pools scale to zero, every Run that lands on an empty pool fails before the autoscaler launches a node.\n\nPlacement: baseline tolerates `workload-type=ci:NoSchedule`, nodeSelector `workload-type: ci`; profiles amd64/arm64 add `kubernetes.io/arch`. CI pools scale to zero; every other node has another `workload-type` taint.\n\nRun 01a1d11d-ca3b-72ba-b653-5463d59cee5d (pipeline ci-tools-image, pull_request). Checkout attempts a1/a2/a3 (18:55:53/:56/:57 UTC) each got FailedScheduling \"0/9 nodes are available: 9 node(s) had untolerated taint(s) … Preemption is not helpful for scheduling.\" Commit status failure at 18:55:59. Karpenter never provisioned: each Pod was deleted before its batch window closed (1s idle, 10s max).\n\ncrates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs, `pod_state`, Pending branch (~6339): when `is_unschedulable(pod)` (PodScheduled=False, reason Unschedulable) holds, it returns `ExecState::Failed { Infra { never_started: true } }` at once. The bounded auto-retry makes a new Pod about 1s later, judged the same way, so the retries are spent in ~4s.\n\nOn an autoscaling cluster Unschedulable is the first state of every Pod that needs a new node: a node is coming.\n\nA step that needs a new node waits while the autoscaler provisions it (Karpenter: 30–90s). A Pod that can never fit still fails with the scheduler's message.\n\n- A grace period before Unschedulable becomes Failed, configurable, a few minutes by default on autoscaling clusters, measured from Pod creation or from PodScheduled=False.\n- And/or read autoscaler signals as Pending: Karpenter `Nominated` (\"Pod should schedule on: nodeclaim/…\") or a NodeClaim created; Cluster Autoscaler `TriggeredScaleUp`.\n- Keep the fast failure when the autoscaler says no node would help (\"incompatible with nodepool\", `NotTriggerScaleUp`).\n\nOne warm CI node per arch. Does not help when a Run needs more than the warm node holds.\n\nKyverno audit (require-resource-limits) flags the checkout Pod's init container for no resources.requests / limits.memory. Audit only.","files":null}]}